WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
A decimal shows parts smaller than one.

2
00:02.000 --> 00:05.600
Cut the whole into 10 equal parts.

3
00:05.600 --> 00:08.600
Shade 3 of the 10 parts.

4
00:08.600 --> 00:11.400
We write 3 tenths as 0.3.

5
00:11.400 --> 00:14.400
The dot separates wholes from parts.

6
00:14.400 --> 00:17.400
0.3 means 0 wholes and 3 tenths.
